Subject: No GPU renderer build of Hex's in kiln's copy
Why: Hex's shards-gpu entry names the files its scripts/shards-gpu/build.sh rebuilds Shards' GPU renderer from; Hex compiles none of them, kiln's copy takes none, and kiln carries no GPU VM process (docs/shards.md), so kiln's copy of Hex's manifest names no such copy of Shards.
Kiln-only: kiln's copy leaves out what only Hex's own scripts build

diff --git a/vendor/MANIFEST.toml b/vendor/MANIFEST.toml
index ff20ca5c4170645f741a4791e7dc5b28408cbb9b..2765ff07f13a2239207946758149128e08a24c91 100644
--- a/vendor/MANIFEST.toml
+++ b/vendor/MANIFEST.toml
@@ -118,24 +118,6 @@ path = "vendor/shards"
 take = ["LICENSE", "AGENTS.md", "CLAUDE.md", "clippy.toml", "rustfmt.toml", "docs/development-rules.md", "docs/development-evidence.md", "crates/api", "crates/abi", "crates/afunix", "crates/dns", "crates/ipc", "crates/remote", "crates/testdir", "docs/research/measurements/managed-borrowed-nowait/focused.rs", "docs/research/measurements/managed-borrowed-nowait/contract.rs", "docs/research/measurements/managed-proc-main/allocation.rs", "docs/research/measurements/managed-proc-main/repro.rs", "docs/research/measurements/managed-proc-main/reader-tests.rs", "docs/research/measurements/api-flakes/spawns.rs", "docs/research/measurements/api-flakes/half-close.rs"]
 own = ["Cargo.toml", "UPSTREAM.md"]
 
-# Hex's `shards` build (hyper-light): the `shards` binary a node boots its Shards guests and image VMs with
-# (SHARDS_BIN; crates/hex-runtime/src/guest), at the same Shards main as vendor/shards, with no change of Hex's: its
-# GPU VM process for Windows on arm64, Hex's last change here, is upstream (9e01ef94a). Hex compiles none of it: the
-# build's files it took for that change are kept, so `check` proves them upstream's at this commit, and
-# scripts/shards-gpu/build.sh rebuilds `shards` from this commit, on Linux, macOS and Windows. MIT, its LICENSE taken
-# beside it.
-[projects.shards-gpu]
-kind = "git"
-repository = "https://github.com/hyper-light/shards"
-commit = "740fa37268c9200616f6fd543d96625953e23b81"
-path = "vendor/shards-gpu"
-take = [
-    "LICENSE",
-    "crates/shards/build.rs",
-    "scripts/gpu-libs",
-]
-own = ["UPSTREAM.md"]
